<section class="three-tool-knowledge" id="hawl-deep-guide">
<h2>Zakat anniversary calculator: hawl, lunar-year dates and complete guide</h2>
<p><strong>Short answer:</strong> A Zakat anniversary is a recurring <em>Hijri</em> review date after a relevant lunar year (<em>hawl</em>) has passed from the point recognised under your religious guidance. It is not 365 days after a salary payment, nor does a calendar alone decide that Zakat is due. <a href="https://www.islamic-relief.org.uk/giving/islamic-giving/zakat/hawl/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Islamic Relief UK's scholar-reviewed hawl explanation</a> describes the lunar-year basis.</p>
